                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0858079-80e3-3d2c-9fd1-8fdc4f158e50",
                                        "entry_id": "d8b994a4-3069-3dae-9134-7fa94708241a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A proponent of the philosophical or logical theories of Aristotle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Aristotelian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f60baffe-c5db-3f4c-9a49-85a1cea8ea4c",
                                        "entry_id": "58adafb2-9bb5-3038-ba02-2d045950a385",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to, or advocating the philosophical or logical theories of Aristotle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "386bdab0-fa45-4006-a1d8-34abae8bfea4",
                                                "sense_id": "f60baffe-c5db-3f4c-9a49-85a1cea8ea4c",
                                                "text": "Having noted that, it should be kept in mind that such scholars (i.e. those who reject that Cusanus is trivialist) should not cite as evidence for denying he was a trivialist the fact that Cusanus was an advocate of Aristotelian logic and the Law of Non-Contradiction. This is because an advocacy of both Aristotelian logic and the law of Non-Contradiction are quite compatible with being a trivialist – the trivialist accepts the truth of all propositions, including the Law of Non-Contradiction and other laws of Aristotelian logic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "57de1603-c8d5-42f7-803a-f09c6d9c2d83",
                        "source_entry_id": "11308ffb-e7bb-3e12-bddf-8549df1591fd",
                        "source_sense_id": "14fe2178-4450-3037-b2a3-933022e8f7e3",
                        "source_sense_description": "ein Anhänger der Lehre des Aristoteles",
                        "target_lang_word": "aristotélicien",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aristotélicien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a2aa37c-6d4f-397d-9f4d-f34e13c4052a",
                                        "entry_id": "26e44dc5-a76f-3fb2-8a9b-d0203aaba70f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est conforme à l’aristotélisme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a79bbf82-f2a1-4ba9-8095-301725d62dca",
                                                "sense_id": "9a2aa37c-6d4f-397d-9f4d-f34e13c4052a",
                                                "text": "L'Encyclopédie aristotélicienne apparut comme la somme de connaissances humaines auxquelles l'esprit humain peut accéder par ses propres forces."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c38eb52b-558f-40f2-8151-73be241f0998",
                                                "sense_id": "9a2aa37c-6d4f-397d-9f4d-f34e13c4052a",
                                                "text": "Loin de paraître comme inconciliables avec la piété, les commentaires nouveaux pouvaient sembler à certains mystiques parisiens un compromis heureux entre le néoplatonisme augustinien, l’abélardisme aristotélicien et l’esprit positif des savants ou des astrologues."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f43d7a7-d45f-47d6-8e18-9ee44b620f23",
                                                "sense_id": "9a2aa37c-6d4f-397d-9f4d-f34e13c4052a",
                                                "text": "Bustamante balaya la remarque d'un revers de main de l'air de dire que la logique aristotélicienne ne s'appliquait pas dans cette affaire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "aristotélicien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46fbc931-a59f-354d-979e-6b9de30a78df",
                                        "entry_id": "0ae1b716-4d93-3bf7-b254-154e40f1c01b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Partisan de la doctrine d’Aristote."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "932eb57b-89b9-4f3b-9080-707fb76326f8",
                                                "sense_id": "46fbc931-a59f-354d-979e-6b9de30a78df",
                                                "text": "Les aristotéliciens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f00578c-3b92-4fac-8fc6-5de80d3550a7",
                                                "sense_id": "46fbc931-a59f-354d-979e-6b9de30a78df",
                                                "text": "Enfin, nous savons par les écrits de Siger de Brabant qu’il est un aristotélicien averroïste, c’est-à-dire un aristotélicien rigide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
